Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 22:19:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 017/159] [ae-patch] Fix the terminal Paste button's review
 findings

Review of patch 0016 (the touch Paste button on the web terminal) found
these, fixed here:

- Paste now goes through pasteIntoAeTerminal, the same guards a Run
  gets: nothing is written unless the socket is open, and multi-line
  text is refused unless the shell turned on bracketed paste, where
  every line would otherwise run as it arrived. Exactly one trailing
  newline (\n or \r\n), a common copy artifact, is dropped first.
- The session is taken at tap time. After the clipboard read, the text
  is written only if that same session is still current and open; a
  terminal that reconnected during the read gets nothing, and the text
  waits in the sheet. A read that resolves after unmount is dropped.
- Every paste that does not go through opens the sheet with the text
  kept and a message for its cause: clipboard unreadable (API missing
  or refused), clipboard empty, terminal not connected, terminal
  reconnected during the read, or multi-line text the shell cannot
  take. Send closes the sheet only on success and otherwise keeps the
  draft and says why.
- TerminalView keeps the control mounted while the attach is writable,
  not only while connected, so an iOS app switch that drops the socket
  no longer destroys an open sheet and its draft; the button is
  disabled while not connected.
- The sheet's DialogContent renders unconditionally, so it animates
  closed like the other dialogs.
- Comments no longer claim the phone's keyboard returns: iOS does not
  raise it from a focus call made after an await.

The suite adds the multi-line refusal and the bracketed pass, the
trailing newline, a replaced or closed session during the read, a
late read after unmount, a Send that cannot write, the empty clipboard,
and a TerminalView test that the control and its sheet outlive a
dropped socket.

